  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "In rhombus \\(ABCD,\\) point \\(P\\) lies on segment \\(\\overline{AD}\\) so that \\(\\overline{BP} \\perp \\overline{AD},\\) \\(AP = 3,\\) and \\(PD = 2.\\) What is the area of \\(ABCD?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\( 3\\sqrt 5 \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\( 10 \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\( 6\\sqrt 5 \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\( 20 \\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\( 25 \\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "d",
    "value": "20"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2022-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(ABCD\\) is a rhombus, \\[AB=AD=AP+PD=5.\\] Right triangle \\(ABP\\) then gives \\[\\begin{aligned}BP&=\\sqrt{AB^2-AP^2}\\\\&=\\sqrt{25-9}=4.\\end{aligned}\\] Thus the rhombus has base \\(AD=5\\) and height \\(BP=4,\\) so its area is \\(5\\cdot4=20.\\)\n\nThus, the answer is D .",
      "hints": [
        "Use the right triangle with legs AP and BP",
        "The altitude from B splits the rhombus side AD"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
